  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN254.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">viṉaimuṟṟi vanteytiya talaimakaṉ ṟērppākaṟkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What HE, who had come back after finishing [his] work, said to the charioteer.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN254.1">
        <l>naraivirā vuṟṟa naṟumeṉ kūntal</l>
        <l>cemmutu ceviliyar palarpā rāṭṭap</l>
        <l>polaṉcey kiṇkiṇi <anchor n="1"/>nalampeṟu cēvaṭi</l>
        <l>maṇaṉmali muṟṟattu nilamvaṭuk koḷ<supplied>ḷā</supplied>a</l>
        <l><anchor n="2"/>maṉaiyuṟai puṟaviṉ ceṅkāṟ cēva</l>
        <l>ṟuṇaiyoṭu kuṟumpaṟai payiṟṟi mēṟcela</l>
        <l>viḷaiyā ṭāyat <anchor n="3"/>tiḷaiyōrk kāṇṭoṟu</l>
        <l>namvayi ṉiṉaiyu naṉṉuta larivai</l>
        <l>pulampoṭu vatiyuṅ kalaṅkaña rakala</l>
        <l>vēntuṟu toḻiloṭu vēṟupulat talki</l>
        <l>vantuviṉai mu<supplied>ṭi</supplied>ttaṉa <anchor n="4"/>māyi ṉīyum</l>
        <l>paṇainilai muṉaiiya viṉainavil puravi</l>
        <l>yiḻaiyaṇi neṭuntē rāḻi yuṟuppa</l>
        <l>nuṇkoṭi miṉṉiṟ paimpayir tumiyat</l>
        <l>taḷava mullaiyoṭu talaiit taṇṇeṉa</l>
        <l><anchor n="5"/>veṟikamaḻ koṇṭa vītatai puṟavi</l>
        <l>ṉeṭiyiṭai <supplied>pi</supplied>ṉpaṭak kaṭavumati yeṉṟiyāṉ</l>
        <l>colliya vaḷavai nīṭātu valleṉat</l>
        <l>tārmaṇi <supplied>mā</supplied>va<supplied>ṟi</supplied> vuṟāa</l>
        <l>vūrnaṇit <anchor n="6"/>tantaṉai yuvakaiyām peṟavē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="10">When, having dwelt in other regions with the task set by the king,</l>
        <l corresp="11a-c">we came [and] finished the work,</l>
        <l corresp="9">so that the stirring grief departs, which abides along with loneliness</l>
        <l corresp="8">in [our] young woman with a good forehead who thinks of us</l>
        <l corresp="7">every time she sees the youths with [her] playmates,</l>
        <l corresp="5">so that the red-legged cock of the dove staying in the house</l>
        <l corresp="6">goes up, flapping(?) [its] short wings, along with [its] mate,</l>
        <l corresp="4">the ground in the courtyard full of sand not taking [any] impression(?)</l>
        <l corresp="3">from the red feet that are beautified by the tinkling anklets made of gold,</l>
        <l corresp="2">while the upright old foster-mother [and] many [others] praise [it, her?],</l>
        <l corresp="1">[her] fragrant soft tresses tinged with white,</l>
        <l corresp="11d 20">you too have brought [us] near the village, for us to obtain joy,</l>
        <l corresp="19">making the horses with bells in a garland feel the knowledge [of our haste]</l>
        <l corresp="18">strongly, without delaying, much as I told [you]:</l>
        <l corresp="17">“drive, for the long way to be behind [us],</l>
        <l corresp="16">in the woodland packed with blossoms that is all fragrant with perfume,</l>
        <l corresp="15">coolly showering golden along with [white] jasmine,</l>
        <l corresp="14">so that the fresh tendrils are cut off, flash-like, from the fine creepers,</l>
        <l corresp="13">when the wheels of the jewel-adorned long chariot caught [them],</l>
        <l corresp="12">with horses trained for [their] task that hated standing in the bamboo.”</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
